Author: Cameron Bytheway <bythewc@amazon.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 22 04:41:02 2026 +0000

    corpus(06-numeric): gate-visible pins for two landed width-descent rejects + baseline a stranded Float32-match case
    
    Adds two gate-visible regression guards for width-fit-descent fixes that already
    landed but had no corpus pin (a --lib-only guard is NOT gate-visible: xtask gate
    runs the spec/semantics corpus, not cargo test -p rcdzc --lib):
    
      - a MULTI-PAYLOAD user sum `(: (P 999 5) P)` over `(P Int8 Int8)` rejects CDZ0302
        (the tuple-zip payload arm — the single-payload newtype twin was already pinned)
      - a contextual FLOAT literal grounded to Float32 through an arith operand
        `(+ a 1.0e300)` overflows to inf and rejects CDZ0201 (the float mirror of the
        UInt8 10000/100 arith-spine pair; the corpus note at the fitting `(+ a 1.5)`
        case already anticipated this pin — reworded it from "filed as a check gap" to
        point at the now-present reject case)
    
    Also baselines a pre-existing but never-baselined passing case ("a bare-literal-arm
    float match under Float32 emits valid f32 across the select and probe-chain paths")
    from an earlier landed Float32 fix — closing the same --lib-not-gate-visible gap.
    
    Verified: gate 4602 pass / 0 fail (wasm), rejects on rust + rust-async too; 0
    regressions vs baseline; ML round-trip 561 ok. Corpus-only, no compiler change.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/spec/semantics/06-numeric-model.sexp b/spec/semantics/06-numeric-model.sexp
index e49d60e92..a4f34a683 100644
--- a/spec/semantics/06-numeric-model.sexp
+++ b/spec/semantics/06-numeric-model.sexp
@@ -582,6 +582,16 @@
   (input  (do (type W (W Int8)) (def (main) (match (: (W 999) W) ((W v) v))) (export main)))
   (error  CDZ0302))
 
+(case "a literal in a MULTI-PAYLOAD user sum that overflows the annotated width is rejected"
+  (doc    "`(type P (P Int8 Int8))` then `(: (P 999 5) P)` — a multi-payload variant boxes its payloads as a
+           tuple, so the descent must zip each declared payload type against its constructor arg: the FIRST
+           arg `999` overflows Int8 → CDZ0302, exactly as the single-payload `(W 999)` above. Pins that the
+           user-sum descent reaches every position of a MULTI-payload variant (the tuple-zip arm), not only
+           the single-payload newtype — a per-position miscompile would otherwise silently truncate the
+           over-range payload (999 → -25 on wasm; rust E0308).")
+  (input  (do (type P (P Int8 Int8)) (def (main) (match (: (P 999 5) P) ((P u _v) u))) (export main)))
+  (error  CDZ0302))
+
 (case "a literal in a RECORD FIELD that overflows the annotated field width is rejected"
   (doc    "`(: (record (x 999)) (Record (: x Int8)))` — the record type's declared field `x : Int8` grounds
            the field literal `999`, which overflows Int8 → CDZ0302, exactly as the Option/user-sum payloads.
@@ -1072,15 +1082,29 @@
            `+` unifies its operand widths, grounding the bare `1.5` at Float32, where it is exactly
            representable in binary32; `2.25 + 1.5` = `3.75` at f32 end-to-end. Pins that a float literal
            grounded by an OPERAND's width (no annotation anywhere) computes at the narrow width. (The
-           OVERFLOWING twin `(+ a 1.0e300)` currently materializes ±inf on both backends instead of
-           rejecting — filed as a check gap; when its reject lands, its case joins this one as the
-           float mirror of the UInt8 10000/100 arith-spine pair.)")
+           OVERFLOWING twin `(+ a 1.0e300)` is the reject case immediately below — the float mirror of the
+           UInt8 10000/100 arith-spine pair.)")
   (input  (do
             (def (main (: a Float32))
               (+ a 1.5))
             (export main)))
   (call   main (: 2.25 Float32)) (output (: 3.75 Float32)))
 
+(case "a FLOAT literal grounded to Float32 through an arith operand overflows to infinity and is rejected"
+  (doc    "The OVERFLOWING float mirror of the UInt8 10000-through-a-spine reject and the fitting `(+ a 1.5)`
+           twin above: `(+ a 1.0e300)` over `(: a Float32)` — the `+` unifies its operand widths, grounding
+           the bare `1.0e300` at Float32, where it OVERFLOWS binary32 (largest finite ~3.4e38) and would
+           become ±inf, a malformed value with no written form. Contextual (no annotation to blame) →
+           CDZ0201, exactly as the integer arith-spine overflow, NOT the annotated CDZ0302. Before the float
+           arith-operand path ran the fits_f32 check it materialized inf on BOTH backends (a silent wrong
+           value); pins that the contextual-grounding fit-check covers FLOAT widths, not only integers — the
+           float face of the arith-spine range check.")
+  (input  (do
+            (def (main (: a Float32))
+              (+ a 1.0e300))
+            (export main)))
+  (error  CDZ0201))
+
 ; A COMPARISON WALLS OFF the arith-spine width climb — the other no-over-rejection face. The arith-spine
 ; fit-check climbs an integer-arith chain because an arith op (`+`/`*`/`%`) unifies its operands to ONE width;
 ; a comparison (`<`) does NOT — its result is `Bool`, so a narrow width sitting only on a comparison's OPERANDS
